SUMMARY:FYI: What’s happenin’
DESCRIPTION:Hendo Fun Friends\n**For Sept 17 thru 25**\n\nUpcoming **music
  events** may be found here:\n[https://www.facebook.com/hendolivemusic/](h
 ttps://www.facebook.com/hendolivemusic/)\n\n**Assorted entertainment\, fes
 tival & market events may be found here:**\n[https://visithendersonvillenc
 .org/calendar-of-events](https://visithendersonvillenc.org/calendar-of-eve
 nts)\n\n**Library programs** may be found here:\n[https://hendersonpl.libc
 al.com/](https://hendersonpl.libcal.com/)\n**Library After Hours**\n**Sept
 ember 25** @ 5:30 pm - 7:00 pm\; Free\nThe Library if officially hosting i
 ts first ever Library After Hours event!\nJoin for an evening of crafts\, 
 library behind the scenes tour\, and a personalized book recommendations p
 anel in an evening tailored for adults in the community! Ask the experts e
 xactly what you should read next based on your personal preferences and di
 scover new titles you may not have heard of before! Even more fun to come.
 \n\\*Please note this is an 18+ only event as this is intended to be an ev
 ening focused for adults. Please enjoy a few kid-free hours at the library
 !\n\n**Rhythm & Brews: Brennen Leigh [Country] with The Dudes [String band
 ]**\nSeptember 17 @ 5:30 pm - 9:00 pm\; Free\n[https://visithendersonville
 nc.org/event/rhythm-brews-brennen-leigh-with-the-dudes](https://visithende
 rsonvillenc.org/event/rhythm-brews-brennen-leigh-with-the-dudes)\n\nFall C
 raft Fair\nSeptember 19 @ 11:30 am - 5:00 pm\n25+ local artists and makers
 \,\nhttps://visithendersonvillenc.org/event/its-fall-yall-craft-fair\n\nSa
 turday\, September 19\nFletcher's Annual Fall Family Festival\n2:30-7:30pm
 \, Bill Moore Community Park\, 300 Old Cane Creek Rd\, Fletcher\nBring the
  whole family out and enjoy an afternoon and evening filled with local ven
 dors\, food trucks\, live music\, kids’ activities\, and a spectacular f
 ireworks finale! Band Schedule: Tracy Davis 2:30-4:30pm and The Showboat B
 and 5:30-7:30pm.\n\nSaturday\, September 19\nFine Line Band\n6-10pm\, J&M 
 Farms\, 3016 Chimney Rock Road\, Hendersonville\n\nSaturday\, September 19
 \nVirginia and The Slims\n7-9pm\, Southern Appalachian Brewery\, 822 Locus
 t St\, Hendersonville\n**Treskas Pollinator Festival**\nSunday\, September
  20th\; 1–7 PM\nSpend your Sunday surrounded by native plants\, local ar
 t\, live music\, foraging\, wildlife education\, and all the little creatu
 res that keep our world blooming!\nat Treska’s @ Highland Lake in Flat R
 ock\nhttps://highlandlakecove.com/so/21Q19T503?languageTag=en&cid=bf667dce
 -2193-4234-8a58-3e71c69a3a66\n**Celtic Harp Concert**\nSeptember 20 @ 4:00
  pm - 5:30 pm\; Free\nFlat Rock\, N.C. – The Friends of Music & the Arts
  Series at the Episcopal Church of St. John in the Wilderness welcomes aut
 umn with a Celtic Harp concert Sunday\, September 20 at 4:00 p.m. Open to 
 the public\, the free concert will be held in the spacious Parish Hall opp
 osite the church at 1905 Greenville Highway\, Flat Rock.\nhttps://visithen
 dersonvillenc.org/event/celtic-harp-concert-opens-new-series-season\nWedne
 sday\, September 23\nJason DeCristofaro's Jazz Night (Each Wednesday)\n6-8
 pm\, Southern Appalachian Brewery\, 822 Locust St\, Hendersonville\n**Libr
 ary After Hours**\nSeptember 25 @ 5:30 pm - 7:00 pm\; Free\nJoin for an ev
 ening of crafts\, library behind the scenes tour\, and a personalized book
  recommendations panel in an evening tailored for adults in the community!
 \nHenderson County Main Library\; 301 N Washington Street\, Hendersonville
 \nhttps://visithendersonvillenc.org/event/library-after-hours\nFriday\, Se
 ptember 25\nKaraoke and dancing with DJ Fr3sh\n7-11pm\, Sissy’s Farm\, 3
 016 Chimney Rock Road\, Hendersonville\n\nThese are NOT hosted events and 
 are posted for informational purposes only. Please make personal arrangeme
 nts to meetup with friends and family.\nIf you wish to attend and host one
  of these events\, I will post the event as an individual happening. Hosti
 ng only requires being focal point for others and making introductions. Si
 mple!!
