SUMMARY:Cataloochee Valley ELK (GSMNP) 
DESCRIPTION:Hendo Fun Friends\nI am going to Cataloochee Valley in the Smo
 ky Mtn Nat'l Pk to explore\, picnic and\, hopefully\, **catch the Elk duri
 ng their 'rut' bugling.** Up to 16 are welcome to join me.\nThis event is 
 suitable for non-hikers and “grade school-age” grandchildren.\n**Since
  the storm destroyed much of the valley road\, we will park near the churc
 h and see how far we can walk into the valley.**\nThe elk usually overnigh
 t in the valley. Usually\, by 4-5pm. There is never a guarantee. But\, if 
 we get lucky\, it's an event not to be missed.\nCataloochee Valley has a h
 istorical home\, church and barn which we will take time to explore.\n**Th
 e plan is to arrive early afternoon to give time to explore and 'PICNIC' b
 efore the elk 'present' themselves.**\nBring a folding chair\, bug spray\,
  camera\, water & food.\nHiking NOT required.\n**We are the Sloth Hike Tea
 m of WNC: “We will get there when we get there.” We dare to go where t
 he ‘real’ hike groups don’t !!**\n**https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=
 Bsh_8qxUfDY**\nTHOSE WHO MIGHT WISH TO DO THIS ‘ON THEIR OWN’ MAY CONT
 ACT ME\, via email (see below)\, FOR EXACT DIRECTIONS. (mid Sep thru-Mid O
 ct).\nDrive time: 1.25 hr/55 mi (one way) Via I-40W to exit 20 (Jonathan C
 reek) **(SMOKY MTN NATL PK PARKING TAGS REQR’D – I WILL CONTACT DRIVER
 S WITH THE INFO).**\n**\\*\\*Special Note\\*\\*:** The last 5 miles of the
  drive are not suitable for low sedans. It is a switchback climb up a moun
 tain gravel road. Those with excessive fear of height or prone to carsickn
 ess will be uncomfortable on this road.\nGoogle Maps: = “Cataloochee Val
 ley – Elk Watching”\nGoogle Maps: = “Palmer Chapel Methodist Church
 ”\n**Return Not earlier than: 7:30 PM**\n**CARPOOL CONTRIBUTIONS APPRECI
 ATED. $7.00 SUGGESTED**\n**DOGS: Since this in in the Smoky Mtn Nat'l Pk\;
  dogs are NOT invited to this event.**\nWeather Check: Jonathan Creek\, NC
 \nWAITLISTED PEOPLE WILL BE ADDED AS DRIVERS SIGN ON.\nI currently have 3 
 driver(s). (=11ppl)\nIncessant prattlers will be assumed to be having an a
 ffair.\nWe suggest slightly open windows while carpooling. Only you know y
 our own health status so judge accordingly if an event may endanger your h
 ealth or the health of others.\nPlease bring an extra pair of shoes to avo
 id bringing your muddy shoes into the driver's car at the end of the hike.
 \nAll hikes are at your own risk. You are responsible for your OWN safety 
 and adequate equipment.\nWaiver: There are certain risks inherent in any o
 utdoor activity. Each participant\, by signing up to attend this event\, a
 grees to release from liability the leader(s)\, Hendo Fun Friends\, its Pa
 rtners\, Affiliates\, and members for any accident\, injury\, illness\, or
  personal loss which might occur while participating in this activity or w
 hile traveling in any vehicle during this trip. Each participant further a
 grees to abide by the rules and regulations concerning safety\, to follow 
 instructions of the leader(s)\, and not to become intentionally separated 
 from the group. The leader(s) also has the right to use any images collect
 ed on this trip for recording on website photo collections.\ngordie's cont
 act: CurmudgeonHiker@gmail.com\n(**before** day of hike): 828.393.0297 (ta
 lk & text)\n**Pics: https://www.flickr.com/photos/146993931@N05/albums**
